            "Nine companies in two groups. There are three ways to win a highway: **EPC**, where the government pays for the road and the builder simply designs, buys the materials and builds it; **HAM** (hybrid annuity model), where the government pays 40% of the cost during building and the rest as annuities over 15 years, so the builder must put in equity and wait; and **toll (BOT or TOT)**, where the developer funds or buys the road and collects tolls for decades, taking the traffic risk.",
